.TH RMDIR 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove empty directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmdir
.IR dir ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rmdir
removes each
.I dir
named, which must be empty. A directory that can't be removed is reported
on standard error as
.BI "rmdir: " dir ": " reason
and the rest are still tried.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every directory was removed (or none was named), 1 if any could not be.
.SH NOTES
There are no options: no
.B \-p
to remove parent directories too.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR rm (1)
